# --- Rust ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `/target*/` rather than `/target/`: cross-linting the workspace for Linux
# uses a separate CARGO_TARGET_DIR so the two platforms do not thrash one
# another's artefacts.
/target*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace produces binaries, and
# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is generated from it. Do not ignore it.

# --- .NET ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Scoped to where MSBuild actually writes, NOT a bare `**/bin/`. Cargo puts
# binary crate roots in `src/bin/`, so the usual .NET pattern would silently
# exclude cli/src/bin/ — both Rust executables — from the repository.
ui/**/bin/
ui/**/obj/
spikes/**/bin/
spikes/**/obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# packages.lock.json IS committed: the dotnet-vuln-scan CI job resolves
# transitive packages from it. Do not ignore it.

# --- Release artefacts --------------------------------------------------
/artifacts/

# --- Catalog signing ----------------------------------------------------
# The Ed25519 secret key must never reach the repository. catalog/pubkey.hex
# is committed on purpose; everything below is not.
*.key
*.sk
secret*.hex
catalog/*.secret*

# --- Observation harness ------------------------------------------------
# Diffs are committed, raw snapshots are not: they contain full path listings
# of a real machine. See docs/16-OBSERVATION-HARNESS.md.
observations/**/*-snapshot.json
observations/**/snapshot-*.json
*.snapshot.json

# --- Editors ------------------------------------------------------------
/.idea/
*.swp
